    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d889">

                <pb facs="1164" n="1154" xml:id="pg1154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.351/3–1346: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-03-13">March 13,
                        1946</date>.<lb/>[Received March 13—3:27 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>424. Following from Dairen received March 13 in clear:</p>
                <p>(Sent to Chungking as No. 182, March 13; repeated to Dept as 424).</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“For the Embassy, Chungking, 2, March 12.</p>
                    <p>Have made preliminary arrangement for reestablishing consular representation
                        Dairen with concurrence of Soviet authorities. Facilities to be made
                        available for communication regarded by authorities as subject for
                        arrangement between respective governments. Question of other consular
                        facilities to be discussed locally after establishment of representation. In
                        course of discussion Commandant indicated necessary consider subject in late
                            [<hi rendition="#italic">light</hi>] existing military situation and
                        within framework of Sino-Soviet treaty.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d889-f1"/>
                        Offered such cooperation and assistance as within powers. Signed
                        Sturgeon.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d889-f1" n="1" xml:id="d889-f1-content">
                <p>Signed at Moscow, August 14, 1945, United Nations Treaty Series, vol. 10, p. 300,
                    or Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">United States Relations With
                        China</hi> (Washington, Government Printing Office, 1949), pp. 585–596.</p>
            </note>
